---
import Accordion from './Accordion.astro';
---

<section id="faq" class="faq">
	<div class="faq__grid wrap">
		<div class="faq__head">
			<h2 class="headline" data-reveal>Common questions <span>about setup</span></h2>
			<p class="lede" data-reveal style="--d:1">
				Still curious? The <a href="/docs/">documentation</a> covers every command and setting.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="faq__list" data-reveal style="--d:2">
			<Accordion question="Do I need a cloud account or subscription?">
				No. Relego is free and open source, and you run it yourself. There is no cloud account, no subscription and no usage limit.
			</Accordion>
			<Accordion question="Which SMTP providers are supported?">
				Any provider with standard SMTP and username and password authentication: AWS SES, Resend, MailerSend, Mailgun or your own mail server. Providers that only allow OAuth, such as Gmail and Outlook, are not supported.
			</Accordion>
			<Accordion question="How often are recaps delivered?">
				Daily at 18:00 with five highlights, unless you change it. Choose daily or weekly at any time of day, and set how many highlights each recap holds, from 1 to 15. You can also send one right now from the web interface or with <code>relego recap trigger</code>.
			</Accordion>
			<Accordion question="Which readers are supported?">
				Relego imports Kindle My Clippings.txt files and Kobo KoboReader.sqlite databases. Kindle readers receive recaps as EPUB through Send-to-Kindle; Kobo readers receive them as an HTML email in their regular inbox.
			</Accordion>
			<Accordion question="Where is my data stored?">
				On your server, in a single SQLite database inside the Docker volume. Kobo databases are copied and read without ever modifying the file on your device.
			</Accordion>
			<Accordion question="Can I exclude specific books or highlights?">
				Yes. Exclude a single highlight, a whole book or every book by an author, from the Library in the web interface or with <code>relego exclude add highlight|book|author &lt;id&gt;</code>. Excluded items stay in your database but never appear in a recap.
			</Accordion>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.faq {
		padding-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 6rem) clamp(6rem, 12vw, 10rem);
	}

	.faq__grid {
		display: grid;
		gap: 3rem;
	}

	.faq__head a {
		color: var(--color-link);
		text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
	}

	.faq__list {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
	}

	@media (min-width: 60rem) {
		.faq__grid {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
			gap: 5rem;
			align-items: start;
		}

		.faq__head {
			position: sticky;
			top: 7rem;
		}
	}
</style>
